      'Failure modes: only what is on screen can occlude, so occluders behind the camera or hidden behind nearer surfaces do nothing; every surface is assumed infinitely thick, so thin things (the columns, the slats of the fluted panel) over-darken what is behind them (the visibility bitmask in Screen-Space GI fixes this); the radius is in world units, so far-away detail gets fewer pixels of AO; and with no velocity buffer, moving objects would drag their old occlusion behind them. When to use it: any 3D hero lit by an environment, where it is often the difference between floating and grounded. GTAO costs the same as SSAO and is more correct, so prefer it.',
